diff --git a/docs/source/whats_new.rst b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
index 0a5f054616..d703528e6d 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@ Bugs
 - With ``optuna=True``, ROC-AUC scoring failed with ``AttributeError: ... has no attribute 'decision_function'`` for classifiers that only provide ``predict_proba`` (skorch/braindecode nets, ``GaussianNB``, ...): optuna-integration's ``OptunaSearchCV`` defines ``decision_function`` unconditionally, so scikit-learn's scorer picked it. ``OptunaSearchCVClassifier`` now exposes it only when the underlying estimator has it, as scikit-learn's ``BaseSearchCV`` does (:gh:`1251` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Hyper-parameter search failed with multi-metric paradigm scorers: a list of metric names (``scorer=["accuracy", "balanced_accuracy"]``) reached ``GridSearchCV`` with ``refit=True`` (scikit-learn requires a metric name), and with ``optuna=True`` every trial failed with ``KeyError: 'test_score'`` because ``OptunaSearchCV`` takes a single scorer. Grid search now refits on the primary (first) metric and Optuna optimises it; all metrics are still reported on the outer folds (:gh:`1252` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`~moabb.evaluations.splitters.LearningCurveSplitter` with ``policy='ratio'`` took an unstratified prefix of the shuffled training pool, so small subsets often missed classes: splits were skipped with a warning, or fitting crashed with ``y contains previously unseen labels`` when a test class was absent from training (multi-class MI, SSVEP). Ratio subsets are now prefixes of a class-interleaved ordering of the same pool: sizes, nesting across sizes and per-permutation randomness are unchanged, and every class is present as soon as the subset holds at least one sample per class (:gh:`1253` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- Saving a fold model (``save_model=True``) for a hyper-parameter search (``GridSearchCV`` / Optuna) over a torch (skorch/braindecode) pipeline pickled the whole search object with the live network instead of using the torch-aware path used for unwrapped pipelines. :func:`moabb.evaluations.utils._save_model_cv` now saves the search's ``best_estimator_`` like an unwrapped pipeline (``save_params`` for the net) and writes ``best_params_<fold>.json``; searches over non-torch pipelines are saved as before (:gh:`1256` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Beetl2021_A` and :class:`moabb.datasets.Beetl2021_B`
   annotating the final phase's test run with the training runs' four-class map.
   ``final_MI_label.txt`` holds the competition's three-class labels, whose class 2
